#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:521
msgid "Git workflow APIs"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:523
msgctxt "/Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:523"
msgid "`Unreleased` - Introduced."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:525
msgid ""
"The APIs in this section cover repository maintenance, releases, history "
"inspection, collaboration, and CI automation. A string or a dense string "
"array is accepted wherever a parameter is documented as `string|string[]`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:529
msgid "Shared result tables"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:531
msgid ""
"Commit information returned by `commit_info()` and `log()` contains `oid`, "
"`message`, `summary`, `author`, `committer`, and `parent_oids`. A signature "
"table contains `name`, `email`, `time_seconds`, and `offset_minutes`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:535
msgid "Integration methods return:"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:547
msgid ""
"Rebase results use `\"rebased\"` or `\"conflicted\"` outcomes and add "
"`current` and `total`. Operations that stop on conflicts can be continued or "
"aborted with the corresponding API."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:551
msgid "Repository and status"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:563
msgid ""
"`status()` and `is_clean()` options are `include_untracked` (default `true`)"
", `include_ignored`, `recurse_untracked_dirs` (default `true`), and `paths`. "
"`GitStatusSummary` contains `root`, `branch`, `head`, `upstream`, `ahead`, "
"`behind`, `clean`, and `entries`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:568
msgid "History and diff"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:578
msgid "`resolve()` returns `oid`, `kind`, and `shorthand`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:579
msgid "`commit_info()` defaults to `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:580
msgid ""
"`log()` accepts `rev`, `max_count` (default `100`), `skip`, `first_parent`, "
"`reverse`, and `paths`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:582
msgid ""
"`diff()` accepts `from`, `to`, `cached`, `paths`, `context_lines` "
"(default `3`), and `find_renames` (default `true`). Without `from` or `to`, "
"it compares the appropriate worktree, index, or HEAD state."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:585
msgid ""
"A diff result contains `patch`, `files_changed`, `insertions`, `deletions`, "
"and `deltas`. Each delta contains `status`, `old_path`, `new_path`, and "
"`binary`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:588
msgid ""
"`describe()` accepts `rev`, `pattern`, `always`, `abbrev` (default `7`), and "
"`dirty_suffix`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:601
msgid "Branches"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:611
msgid ""
"`branches()` accepts `kind = \"local\" | \"remote\" | \"all\"`; the default "
"is `\"local\"`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:613
msgid ""
"Branch information contains `name`, `kind`, `oid`, `head`, `upstream`, "
"`ahead`, and `behind`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:615
msgid ""
"`branch_create()` accepts `start_point`, `force`, `checkout`, `upstream`, "
"and `confirm`. The default start point is `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:617
msgid ""
"`branch_delete()` accepts `force` and `confirm`. Deleting the current branch "
"fails, and deleting an unmerged branch requires `force = true`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:619
msgid "`branch_rename()` accepts `force` and `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:620
msgid ""
"Pass `nil` to `branch_set_upstream()` to remove an upstream. Its options "
"only contain `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:623
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:631
msgid ""
"`tag_create()` targets `HEAD` by default. Without `message` it creates a "
"lightweight tag; with `message` it creates an annotated tag. Options are "
"`message`, `tagger`, `force`, and `confirm`. A tagger uses the shared "
"signature fields."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:636
msgid ""
"Tag information contains `name`, `oid`, `target_oid`, `target_kind`, "
"`annotated`, `message`, and `tagger`. `tags(pattern)` uses Git's glob "
"matching. Deleting a tag only changes the local repository; delete a remote "
"tag with an explicit push refspec."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:648
msgid "Remotes and transfer"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:662
msgid ""
"Remote information contains `name`, `url`, `push_url`, `fetch_refspecs`, and "
"`push_refspecs`. `remote_add()` accepts `push_url` and `confirm`. "
"`remote_set_url()` accepts `push = true` to change the push URL instead of "
"the fetch URL. Remove, rename, and set URL operations accept `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:667
msgid ""
"`fetch()` accepts `refspecs`, `auth`, `depth`, `prune`, `tags`, "
"`update_fetchhead`, and `confirm`. `push()` accepts `auth`, `force`, "
"`set_upstream`, and `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:671
msgid ""
"`pull()` defaults to remote `\"origin\"`, the current branch, and `strategy "
"= \"ff_only\"`. It also accepts `strategy = \"merge\" | \"rebase\"`, the "
"fetch options `auth`, `depth`, `prune`, `tags`, and `update_fetchhead`, plus "
"`signature`, `message`, and `confirm`. Pull requires a clean repository "
"before it starts."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:677
msgid "Worktree, index, and recovery"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:687
msgid ""
"`restore()` accepts `source` (default `\"HEAD\"`), `staged`, `worktree`, and "
"`confirm`. When only `staged = true` is specified, the worktree is not "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:690
msgid ""
"`reset()` accepts `mode = \"soft\" | \"mixed\" | \"hard\"`, `force`, and "
"`confirm`. A hard reset requires `force = true`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:692
msgid "`remove()` accepts `cached`, `force`, and `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:693
msgid ""
"`clean()` accepts `dry_run`, `force`, `dirs`, `ignored`, `paths`, and "
"`confirm`. It defaults to `dry_run = true`. Actual deletion requires both `"
"dry_run = false` and `force = true`. Directories are left untouched unless `"
"dirs = true`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:703
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:712
msgid ""
"`scope` is `\"local\"`, `\"global\"`, or `\"system\"`; the default for reads "
"is the highest-priority available value and the default for writes is `"
"\"local\"`. Configuration entries contain `name`, `value`, and `scope`. "
"System configuration is read-only. Global `config_set()` and "
"`config_remove()` require `confirm = true` and always show a confirmation "
"prompt."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:718
msgid "Merge, cherry-pick, and revert"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:732
msgid ""
"`merge()` accepts `ff = \"allow\" | \"only\" | \"never\"`, `signature`, "
"`message`, and `confirm`. Merge, cherry-pick, and revert require a clean "
"repository before they start so abort can safely restore `ORIG_HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:736
msgid ""
"Cherry-pick and revert accept `commit` (default `true`), `signature`, "
"`message`, `mainline`, and `confirm`. Set `commit = false` to update the "
"index and worktree without creating a commit. Abort methods accept `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:740
msgid "Stash and rebase"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:753
msgid ""
"Stash indices default to `0`. `stash_save()` accepts `include_untracked`, "
"`include_ignored`, `keep_index`, `signature`, and `confirm`. Apply and pop "
"accept `reinstate_index` and `confirm`; drop accepts `confirm`. Stash "
"information contains `index`, `message`, and `oid`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:758
msgid ""
"`rebase()` requires `upstream` and accepts `onto`, `branch` "
"(default `\"HEAD\"`), `signature`, and `confirm`. The first version supports "
"non-interactive pick operations; interactive squash, fixup, reword, and edit "
"operations are not available. Continue accepts `signature` and `confirm`; "
"abort accepts `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:763
msgid "Advanced repositories"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:778
msgid ""
"Worktree information contains `name`, `path`, `locked`, `lock_reason`, and "
"`valid`. Add options are `reference`, `lock`, `checkout_existing`, and "
"`confirm`. Prune options are `valid`, `locked`, `working_tree`, `force`, and "
"`confirm`; lock and unlock also accept `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:782
msgid ""
"Submodule information contains `name`, `path`, `url`, `branch`, `head_oid`, "
"`index_oid`, and `workdir_oid`. Init options are `overwrite`, `recursive`, "
"and `confirm`. Update options are `init`, `recursive`, `allow_fetch`, `auth`"
", and `confirm`. Sync options are `recursive` and `confirm`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:786
msgid "Recursive submodule processing is disabled unless `recursive = true`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:787
msgid ""
"`blame()` accepts `newest`, `oldest`, `min_line`, `max_line`, `first_parent`"
", copy/move tracking flags, `ignore_whitespace`, and `use_mailmap`. Each "
"hunk contains `final_start_line`, `original_start_line`, `line_count`, "
"`commit_oid`, `author`, `origin_path`, and `boundary`."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:792
msgid "Safety and compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:794
msgid ""
"All mutating methods that accept `confirm` default it to `false`. `force` "
"and `confirm` express different intent: `force` enables behavior that is "
"otherwise rejected, while `confirm` asks the user before an already-valid "
"action runs."
msgstr ""

#: /Users/peterlits/Proj/PeterlitsZo/worktrees/ptool/full-lantern/ptool/website/docs/lua-api/git.md:798
msgid ""
"Existing defaults remain compatible: the default remote is `\"origin\"`, "
"push without refspecs pushes the current branch, status includes untracked "
"files, and empty commits remain allowed unless `allow_empty = false` is "
